:: Second Boss Confrontation [event mom_quest] {"position":"3275,700","size":"100,100"}
<<silent>><<SetBackground "images/locations/reception.jpg">><</silent>>
By now the lobby feels almost familiar. Same marble, same lighting, same receptionist, who glances up from her screen and waves me through before I've even reached the desk.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs to [
    { who: "Receptionist", text: "Floor 6. I'm starting to think you work here." },
    { who: $player, text: "Give it time." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<linkreplace "Take the elevator up">>
<<silently>><<SetBackground "images/locations/elevator.jpg">><</silently>>
This time I spend the elevator ride with the prototype in my hand instead of my pocket, turning it over and over. I've been recalibrating it every night since he laughed at me, and the error hasn't come back once in testing. Then again, I haven't tested it on anyone quite as pleasant as him.

<<linkreplace "Arrive at floor 6...">>
<<silently>><<SetBackground $locations[12].img>><</silently>>
The doors open, and the first thing I see is $mom.callName.

She's wearing what we talked about. A white blouse with one button more undone than she'd ever choose on her own, a fitted brown skirt with a slit up the side, her hair loose over one shoulder. She's bent over a notebook, writing fast, and every few seconds she tugs at her neckline without seeming to notice she's doing it.

<<Video "images/characters/mom/events/second boss confrontation/mom_outfit.mp4" "" "" 500>>

When she spots me, her face does two things at once: relief, and a flush that climbs all the way up to her ears.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs to [
    { who: $player, text: "Hey. You look nice today." },
    { who: $mom, text: "Oh, don't, I already feel like the whole floor is staring at me." },
    { who: $player, text: "Are they?" },
    { who: $mom, text: "Well, some of them. Gary from IT walked into a door. But honey, it actually worked, he hasn't raised his voice once all day, and this morning he told me I seem 'more engaged', whatever that's supposed to mean." },
    { who: $player, text: "Told you. Are you okay in it, though?" },
    { who: $mom, text: "It's a little drafty, but if it keeps the peace I can live with drafty. What are you doing here, anyway? Did you eat?" },
    { who: $player, text: "I ate. I'm just checking on you, and I wanted to have a quick word with him, if he's in." },
    { who: $mom, text: "He's in. Be polite, okay? He's in a good mood for once, and I'd love for it to last until at least Friday." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She squeezes my wrist as I pass, a little thank-you squeeze. She thinks she owes me for a good day.

I knock on his door once and walk in. The prototype is already running in my pocket, the dial turned somewhere I've never tried before, aimed at whatever he keeps behind that smirk. <<UseQuestDevice $mom>> He looks up, annoyed for about half a second, and then visibly amused.

<<linkreplace "Walk further in">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs to [
    { who: $boss, text: "Well, look who's back. The kid with the calculator. What do you want this time?" },
    { who: $player, text: "Did you notice $mom.name today?" },
    { who: $boss, text: "Hard not to. She finally dressed like she wants to keep her job. Why?" },
    { who: $player, text: "Because that was me. I talked her into it last night." },
    { text: "That gets his attention. He sets his pen down and actually looks at me, properly, for the first time." },
    { who: $boss, text: "You talked her into it. Huh. She won't let me finish a sentence, and her kid gets her into a skirt like that in one evening." },
    { who: $player, text: "She listens to me. That's sort of what I came to talk about." },
    { who: $boss, text: "Go on." },
    { who: $player, text: "I'm kind of guessing here, but I don't think you want her on this floor much longer, not if she keeps saying no to you. And you can't just fire her without it getting messy. I'd like her working for me instead, so maybe there's a way we both get what we want." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

The hum in my pocket is so faint I can barely feel it, but I can see it working. His shoulders loosen, and the smirk turns into something hungrier and more honest, like he's just decided I might be worth his time after all.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs to [
    { who: $boss, text: "You want me to fire your own $mom.relation so you can hire her." },
    { text: "He laughs, and for once it doesn't sound like he's laughing at me." },
    { who: $boss, text: "That's the first interesting thing anyone's said in this office all year. All right, kid. If I let her go, it has to be clean, because I'm not spending next spring in a deposition. Five thousand, cash, so I know you're serious. And a video. Her, alone, enjoying herself. You live there, you'll figure it out. Call it a going-away present." },
    { who: $player, text: "And the clean part?" },
    { who: $boss, text: "That's your job, too. Get into her laptop. Delete a few files, scramble her calendar, make her look sloppy. I'll do the rest in front of everybody, and no lawyer on earth will touch it." },
    { text: "He says it the way other people order lunch. I think about the five thousand, which is most of what I have, and about her laptop sitting on her nightstand every night." },
    { who: $player, text: "Okay. Deal." },
    { who: $boss, text: "And kid? If any of this comes back to me, I'll make sure the only thing anybody in this town remembers about your $mom.relation is that video." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<linkreplace "Take the elevator down">>
<<silently>><<SetBackground "images/locations/elevator.jpg">><</silently>>
On the way out I walk past $mom.callName's desk. She gives me a little wave and mouths //thank you//. I wave back.

The elevator is empty. I lean against the mirrored wall and make a list in my head, because lists are easier than thinking about what's on them. Five thousand from my savings, which is going to hurt. A clip, which means waiting outside her door one night with my phone and the prototype. And her laptop, late, when the house is asleep.

Then she gets fired, and she comes home with nowhere to go, and I'll be standing in the hallway with a job offer, if he actually keeps his end of it.

Downstairs the receptionist wishes me a nice day, and I tell her I'm having one.

<<UpdateStat "+" "Corruption" 5>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "MomCorruption" 2>>
<<NextQuest $mom>>
